    "root_cause_category": "expired_credential",
    "explanation": "The TLS certificate for ledger-gateway.internal.example expired, and that is what triggered this incident. Its not_after was 2026-11-12T00:00:00Z (LOG-0002-0016). Four seconds later, payments-worker started failing every upstream call with 'TLS handshake failed: certificate has expired' (LOG-0002-0010 and the repeats after it). Each failing batch was retried, then moved to the dead-letter queue. The settlement error rate hit 97% (LOG-0002-0032) and the settlements queue backed up. The certificate wasn't renewed in time because cert-renewer's DNS validation timed out on 11-10 and 11-11, and it gave up after its maximum attempts (LOG-0002-0001, -0002, -0003). The renewer failing is the reason the certificate lapsed, but the expired certificate itself is the trigger: putting a valid one in place would end the incident. TKT-0002 confirms that no settlements have been confirmed since just after midnight UTC. The GC pauses in the logs were minor and are unrelated.",
